{"agent_id":"pp3g-deeO-re-check-light-review-of-the-revised-remediation-plan","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-14T23:13:15.822492541Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ee70ffad-a783-40c8-9172-67197002f0c9","comment_uuid":"6e05f52f-f80f-4d67-bf61-a3d0faa580eb","author":"pp3g-deeO-re-check-light-review-of-the-revised-remediation-plan","content":"## Review Summary: APPROVED — C1-C4 resolved in revised plan #365\n\nRE-CHECK (light review) of the #365 revised remediation plan against my round-1 blockers (M1/M2/M3) and folds S1-S7. Read-only verification against fork source and disk state. Verdict: APPROVED; all four blockers C1-C4 are resolved with mechanically sound, source-verified resolutions. Non-blocking follow-ups below.\n\n## MUST FIX (blocking)\n- None.\n\n## C1 (M1, B4 init sequence) — RESOLVED. Fork source verified:\n- Plain init no-op on initialized repo (mod.rs:869-874); --update skips deleted (mod.rs:683-687); ONLY --force writes — confirmed, so naming --force explicitly fixes the mechanics.\n- --force collateral verified exactly as claimed: embedded hook-config written (mod.rs:990), ALL 31 RULE_FILES rewritten incl. global/knowledge/project (mod.rs:1045-1059; resources/crosslink/rules has 31 files, no kickoff/tooling), root .gitignore managed section (mod.rs:1040 + merge.rs:57-91), .mcp.json MERGED not overwritten (mod.rs:1131-1132 + merge.rs:96-152; no-op for identical server sets — embedded 381B/3 servers == Tools 453B/3 servers).\n- Non-TTY --force works without --defaults: TUI falls back to defaults (walkthrough.rs:498-502), TuiChoices::default is embedded-derived (mod.rs:78-99). Restore-set need is REAL for ASES/tripn (ASES hook-config 5102B/global 10.2K/knowledge 2.8K/project 1.1K vs embedded 1868B/9.7K/1.7K/274B — all differ) and BENIGN for Tools (only global.md differs: 10188B vs 9893B; knowledge/project binary identical; hook-config semantically identical field-by-field). Drop-rm + git-restore + post-init hash verify is the right call; git-restore is valid because the restore-set files are the tracked files the step-0 baseline commit protects.\n- Test citations verified: test_run_already_initialized_no_force:1334, test_run_force_updates_rules:1633, test_update_skips_deleted_files:2527.\n\n## C2 (M2, B3 enforcement) — RESOLVED (design-level, WNT honest that the consumer check is not yet implemented):\n- Host mechanism verified: tool.execute.before hooks exist (Tools :786, ASES :967 = plan citation, tripn :854); ensureState lazily resolves (ASES :833, plan cited :829 — 4-line drift, NIT); ASES and tripn opencode.json both load the 3 plugins explicitly by name (lines 5-7) — so the consumer check can hash the exact loaded files.\n- Marker-role separation (source canonical manifest TRACKED vs per-destination marker GITIGNORED, consumer READ-only), one-directionality made explicit with --check (both drift classes) + bidirectional --pull (NC-6), and the State 0/1/2 machine with --promote-requires-clean---check + corrupt-in-State-2 fail-closed / missing-marker fail-open are all operational and mechanically grounded. Marker-gitignore 'outside the managed section' survives init --force (verified merge.rs:65-87 only replaces the marked section).\n- Plugin today has NO marker logic (grep: zero matches for marker/promote/state) — consistent with WNT; the cheapest discriminating tests cover the transition.\n\n## C3 (M3, step-0/B5 conflict) — RESOLVED:\n- Tools untracked .opencode/, .worktrees/, .claude/findings-interrupt-plugin.md all exist and NONE are gitignored (Tools/.gitignore = managed section only) — but all are OUTSIDE the narrowed write-set precondition, so the self-contradiction is gone.\n- Step 0 commits global.md ONLY (annotated baseline, never-sync-source) and lets step-1 replacement carry scripts/claude (S4) — verified the deltas are real: Tools global.md 10188B vs embedded 9893B; Tools scripts/claude :68/:70 carry the literal-quote bug, and live ~/.local/bin/claude (3039B) fixes it with --agent :17, --auto :22, CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE :76, correct \"$PROMPT\" :80 — so the canonicalization direction is correct.\n\n## C4 (B5 transaction machinery) — RESOLVED:\n- No sync-tooling.sh anywhere (Tools/scripts, ASES/scripts checked); no .sync-state/.sync-backup/.sync-tmp in Tools. Git-only atomicity, always-overwrite canonical/marker-state, REFUSE+fail-loudly on local edits, per-destination operator commits, no --rollback — coherent and consistent with per-repo git reality. S5/N-1 moot correctly.\n\n## Folds — all disposed; spot-verified:\n- S2 tripn strictness verified (comment_discipline=required :186, signing_enforcement=enforced :220, git worktree remove blocked :59).\n- S6 28/31 allowlist = 31 RULE_FILES minus 3 layer-owned — consistent.\n- NEW skills-inversion fold verified exactly (Tools 4077B vs ASES 6571B crosslink-subagent-orchestration; crosslink-adversarial-review 2984B identical). Wrapper sizes all verified (3039/3639/1498/5853/5853).\n\n## SHOULD CONSIDER (non-blocking)\n- The C1 post-init verify (b) scopes git-clean to restore-set paths, but --force ALSO rewrites the root .gitignore managed section, and the pinned fork's section has 5 MORE entries than the committed one (.last-hydrated-ref, .promoted-uuids, promotion-log.json, hub-v3-shadow-stats.json, sentinel.log — merge.rs:23-27 vs committed 18 entries). Tools' .gitignore WILL show a diff after init --force. The plan tolerates it (outside verify scope) but should document it as an expected, intentional delta so the operator doesn't misread the dirty tree as restore failure.\n- The C3 write-set/manifest ambiguity: Tools/plugins also contains dynamic-models.js, dynamic-models.ts, plugin.ts (model-hiding/cache plugin) which are NOT in the write-set and NOT present in destinations (ASES/tripn opencode.json load only the 3 guards). The manifest source is the whole Tools/plugins dir — either scope the manifest to the 3 guard files (matching the write-set) or explicitly decide the extras' fate.\n- C1 restore/verify does not mention .claude/skills: --force rewrites 18 bundled skills (mod.rs:1119-1129) under Tools/.claude/skills (fork bundle has 18 skills; the 2 crosslink skills are NOT bundled, so no crosslink-skill clobber). These appear to be untracked deploy artifacts — state that explicitly so the operator knows the post-init tree is expected to show them rewritten.\n\n## NITS\n- Byte-size claim '2041B both' is imprecise as stated: embedded raw = 1868B, Tools raw = 2042B. The figure holds only as a re-serialized equivalence (the --force TUI path writes pretty-printed output), not as raw file size. Recommend citing raw sizes + the re-serialized-equivalence framing.\n- ensureState citation :829 vs actual :833 (ASES copy).\n- Plan's fork binary identity 0.9.0-beta.1+37789b51-dirty not independently verifiable read-only (cannot execute the binary).\n\n## WHAT-NOT-TESTED\n- Could not run git status / git ls-files in Tools/ASES/tripn (read-only sandbox denies git execution). The 'git-tracked' and 'dirty-state' claims are supported by file-level evidence (content diffs vs embedded, .gitignore absence of ignore patterns, directory existence, step-0 commit rationale) but not by direct git verification. Recommend the operator confirm restore-set files are tracked (git ls-files) before executing step 5a.\n- Did not execute crosslink init --force (would write files; read-only role). All init-behavior conclusions are from fork source + its tests, exactly as the plan's WNT states.\n- Did not build or run sync-tooling.sh (does not exist yet — design only per plan WNT); state machine + --promote behavior are specified, not executed.\n- Contract battery / plugin load tests not executed (live-env tool execution denied).","created_at":"2026-08-14T23:13:15.812290559Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:IwEldNSB/uxjBaWIqzpLTxHu10cCq/JAI6vhi5mJwI4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPREC9DNnhFgIcqH7nTiNRoqqBe1I+yBYEJJ9aQWhHdoAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAA